### Adding Attributes to a Document Object

#### Overview

To add attributes to a document object, you can use various methods provided by the `Document` class, such as `addAttribute`, `setAttribute`, or `getAttributes`.

#### Methods for Adding Attributes

*   `addAttribute(String key, String value)`: Adds an attribute with the specified key and value.
*   `setAttribute(String key, String value)`: Sets the value of a specific attribute.
*   `getAttributes()`: Returns a map containing all attributes.

#### Example Code

```java
import org.w3c.dom.Document;
import org.w3c.dom.Element;

// Create a new document object
Document doc = createDocument();

// Create an element for testing
Element form = createElement("form");

// Add attributes to the element
doc.addAttribute(form, "id", "test-id");
doc.addAttribute(form, "class", "test-class");

// Set values of specific attributes
doc.setAttribute("style", "test-style");
doc.setAttribute("class", "test-class");

// Print the updated document object
System.out.println(doc);
```

### Adding Attributes to a Form Element

#### Overview

To add attributes to a form element, you can use the `addAttribute` method provided by the `FormElement` class.

#### Methods for Adding Attributes

*   `addAttribute(String key, String value)`: Adds an attribute with the specified key and value.
*   `setAttribute(String key, String value)`: Sets the value of a specific attribute.
*   `getAttributes()`: Returns a map containing all attributes.

#### Example Code

```java
import org.w3c.dom.Document;
import org.w3c.dom.Element;

// Create a new form element
Element form = createElement("form");

// Add attributes to the form element
doc.addAttribute(form, "id", "test-id");
doc.addAttribute(form, "class", "test-class");

// Set values of specific attributes
doc.setAttribute("style", "test-style");
doc.setAttribute("class", "test-class");

// Print the updated document object
System.out.println(doc);
```

### Adding Attributes to a Document Object and Form Element

#### Overview

To add attributes to both a document object and a form element, you can use the `addAttribute` method.

#### Methods for Adding Attributes

*   `addAttribute(String key, String value)`: Adds an attribute with the specified key and value.
*   `setAttribute(String key, String value)`: Sets the value of a specific attribute.
*   `getAttributes()`: Returns a map containing all attributes.

#### Example Code

```java
import org.w3c.dom.Document;
import org.w3c.dom.Element;

// Create a new document object
Document doc = createDocument();

// Create an element for testing
Element form = createElement("form");

// Add attributes to both the document and form elements
doc.addAttribute(form, "id", "test-id");
doc.addAttribute(form, "class", "test-class");

// Set values of specific attributes
doc.setAttribute("style", "test-style");
doc.setAttribute("class", "test-class");

// Print the updated document object
System.out.println(doc);

// Print the updated form element
System.out.println(form);
```

